gosh seam 01: Each end says what it can do, in mosh's own instruction.

For:   REQ10/SHAPE-1, REQ8/CMD-3. A stock mosh must never be sent anything it would misread, and a
       user must be told what the other end cannot do. So before gosh sends anything of its own it
       has to know the other end is a gosh; this is how it is told.
What:  an optional field, capabilities, in Instruction (field 8; an end that does not know the
       field ignores it). The sender holds the value and puts it in each instruction when it is
       not zero; a change in it makes a new instruction; the receiver keeps what the peer said
       (peer_can). Nothing sets it yet, so with this patch alone nothing on the wire changes.
Where: transportinstruction.proto; TransportSender (its constructor and send_in_fragments);
       Fragmenter::make_fragments; Transport (its constructors and recv).
Kind:  additions only. No line of the core is moved or reshaped.
Pin:   upstream mosh at decd9b705eb81626f694335b8d5940538beb06da; cut against the result of the patch before it.
From:  the fork, wmacevoy/mosh at mosh-1.4.0-pf.7; the text added is the fork's, unchanged.

